{"seq": 21, "t": 28.207, "type": "plan", "escalation": false, "diagnosis": "Tests fail to collect because they import `BaseSettings` from `pydantic`, but in v2 it moved to the separate `pydantic-settings` package. The application code in `vault_settings.py` also uses several deprecated APIs: `BaseSettings`, `parse_obj_as`, `__fields__`, and `ValidationError` from old locations, plus behavior changes for `field.alias` and Optional/Nullable field logic.", "dependency_changes": ["Add pydantic-settings>=2,<3 to requirements.txt"], "steps": [{"file": "src/pydantic_vault/vault_settings.py", "change": "Replace `from pydantic import BaseSettings, SecretStr, ValidationError, parse_obj_as` with `from pydantic import SecretStr, ValidationError` and `from pydantic_settings import BaseSettings`; add `from pydantic import TypeAdapter` for parse_obj_as replacement", "rules": ["R55", "R61", "R53", "R88", "R134", "R347"], "why": "BaseSettings moved to pydantic-settings; ValidationError moved to top-level pydantic; parse_obj_as deprecated in favor of TypeAdapter.validate_python"}, {"file": "src/pydantic_vault/vault_settings.py", "change": "Replace `parse_obj_as(bool, _vault_certificate_verify)` with `TypeAdapter(bool).validate_python(_vault_certificate_verify)` at line 97", "rules": ["R53", "R88", "R134", "R347"], "why": "parse_obj_as deprecated; TypeAdapter.validate_python is the v2 equivalent for non-BaseModel validation"}, {"file": "src/pydantic_vault/vault_settings.py", "change": "Replace `settings.__fields__.values()` with `settings.model_fields.values()` at line 270", "rules": ["R1"], "why": "__fields__ renamed to model_fields in v2"}, {"file": "src/pydantic_vault/vault_settings.py", "change": "At line 321, change `d[field.alias] = vault_val` to guard against None: `if field.alias is not None: d[field.alias] = vault_val`", "rules": ["R20"], "why": "In v2, field.alias returns None when not explicitly set (v1 returned the field name)"}, {"file": "src/pydantic_vault/vault_settings.py", "change": "Review Optional[str] and Optional[Dict] fields (lines 43-44) for v2 nullable/required semantics; may need Field(default=None) or validation adjustments", "rules": ["R46"], "why": "V2 changed Optional/Required/Nullable logic to match dataclasses; defaults and validation order may differ"}, {"file": "src/pydantic_vault/vault_settings.py", "change": "Check TypedDict usage (line 17) and dataclass-like inputs for tuple vs dict validation changes", "rules": ["R22"], "why": "Dataclass fields no longer accept tuples as validation inputs in v2"}], "risks": ["BaseSettings in pydantic-settings may have different default behavior for env_file_encoding, case_sensitive, or env_prefix", "ValidationError import path change is straightforward but confirm no custom error handling relies on old module", "Optional field defaults may now be treated as nullable vs required differently; test edge cases with None vs missing env vars", "field.alias returning None may break any serialization that expects the field name as fallback", "__post_init__ now runs after validation (R23) \u2014 if vault_settings uses __post_init__, initialization order changes"]}
